lazydash patch to CoMotion, applied after 0001 by external/bootstrap_comotion.sh.
Exact culls (validity answers unchanged; only fewer primitive tests):

1. Fcl backend: a capsule test before each robot-vs-environment pair. A
   cylinder lies inside the capsule around its axis segment (a sphere is a
   capsule of length 0), so a primitive whose bounding sphere misses that
   capsule cannot touch it. Thin long cylinders (the converted shelf boards
   and wall plates) have bounding spheres far larger than themselves, and FCL
   fits an OBB/RSS to the shape on every mesh-vs-shape call; that fitting was
   85% of the motion query on double_shelf2-4.
2. Spheres backend: isValidSingle tests the robot's bounding sphere against
   each obstacle once, then only the obstacles that reach it against each
   sphere (was every sphere x every obstacle; 63% of layer 2 on wall-8-6-4).
3. Spheres backend: isSelfCollisionFree reads the self-collision mask
   directly (RobotModel::selfCollisionMask) instead of a call per pair.

